# XSH putc()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.

assertion  XSH.putc.001
anchor     functions/putc.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/fputc.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      1988
says       On a stream opened "w", putc('h') returns 'h' and putc(0x1ff)
           returns 0xff; after fclose() the file holds the two bytes 'h'
           and 0xff.
test       t/001-writes.c

assertion  XSH.putc.002
anchor     functions/putc.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/fputc.html#ERRORS/EBADF
class      required
says       On an unbuffered stream opened "w" whose descriptor was closed,
           putc() returns EOF, sets errno to EBADF and sets the stream's
           error indicator.
note       Where setvbuf() refuses _IONBF, the test writes until a call
           fails (the buffer then needs flushing); if none does within
           4 MiB the result is UNRESOLVED.
test       t/002-ebadf.c
